	(text "PWR_FLAG: these rails reach their loads only through passive parts (the edge fingers, USB-C, the P-FET, the SS34, the buck's inductor)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 66.04 195.58 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "db8adcbe-302e-5a94-8192-6cee6073b885")
	)
	(text "Power tree.  CONS_5V is the console's 7805 through the edge fingers: about 480 mA peak (the S3 transmitting through the buck),\n180 mA average.  Q2 AO3401A (D = CONS_5V, S = +5V, G = VBUS) is fully on without USB, so the 74HCT glue sees VCC >= 4.5 V\n(a Schottky drop here would leave no margin); with USB in, its gate goes high and only its body diode conducts, so nothing\nback-feeds the console.  D1 SS34 puts USB VBUS onto +5V.  It is reverse-biased whenever the console powers the cart, and its\nleakage (0.5 mA at 25 C, 20 mA at 100 C) flows into VBUS, the FET gate: R3 4.7k holds VGS at -2.8 V up to 500 uA\n(tools/audit/spice_checks.py).  +5V feeds the 5V glue and both SRAMs (cart-bus), the AP2112K LDO -> +3V3_RP (every RP2354B\nsupply pin: it rises with the console rail, so the 5V-tolerant pads are never unpowered with 5V on them) and the AP63203\nbuck -> +3V3 (ESP32-S3, microSD, CP2102N).  TP14, TP11, TP2, TP7 and the rp-core DVDD pad are bring-up test points."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 66.04 58.42 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "5262b653-5d46-52fd-ba4b-c7512acd43d0")
	)
